Review notes from Cursor (review, CLEAN):
  The exploratory whole-pool path matches the acceptance criteria. Serial flake8 and the full pytest suite both passed on this tree, the 2025 holdout cohort is not loaded, and the README now states that the primary evaluation has already been run.
  
  The exploratory command reads only the configured cohorts 2018, 2019, and 2021–2024 (`YEARS` in `triage_experiment.py`). It never opens `data/cohorts/2025.json`, never constructs the HTTP client, and never sends a season-2026 stats request. Season 2025 statistics are read only as the following-season outcomes for the 2024 cohort, which is the same boundary the primary evaluation uses. A stats file labeled 2026 raises `ValueError` instead of being requested. `guard_outcome_build` is called with those cohort years, so the 2025 holdout lock is not entered.
  
  Published aggregates line up with the primary report. The 2024 whole pool is N=636 with 91 positives and base rate 0.143082, the same whole-pool row as in `research/EXPERIMENT.md`. The selected comparator is B0 because its top-50 hits (32) beat B2 (20), B1 (24), and P (25), which is the documented tie order B2, B0, B1, P. The inference line “M had 38 top-50 hits and B0 had 32” matches `research/exploratory_whole_pool.json`. That JSON has no `person_id` or name fields. Re-running `triage_cli evaluate` still replaces `EXPERIMENT.md` from `validation.json` alone, so the README warning about restoring the exploratory section is accurate.
  
  The README sentence that said the evaluation stage had not been run is gone. The replacement is consistent with `research/validation.json` and the primary report: evaluation ran, stopped on the preregistered rule (23 primary positives, minimum 30), and did not evaluate the 2025 holdout. There is no `noqa`, no flake8 config, and no raised line limit. Quote and wrapping edits in the probe and triage modules are formatting-only; the suite still asserts exact report rendering, holdout guards, and the season-2026 stats rejection.
  
  HowlPlane’s check on this tree was `python3 -m flake8 -j1 cubs_edge_lab tests && python3 -m pytest -q`, exit 0: 69 passed, 5 subtests passed. This review did not re-run that command or git. `research/validation.json` is not in the uncommitted diff. `research/EXPERIMENT.md` and `research/exploratory_whole_pool.json` were already dirty and were left untouched; the passing hash and “primary markdown equals `render(validation.json)`” tests lock the primary section.
  
  Uncommitted files covered by that tree: `README.md`, `cubs_edge_lab/exploratory_whole_pool.py`, the probe modules, `triage.py`, `triage_cli.py`, `triage_config.py`, `triage_eval.py`, `triage_experiment.py`, `triage_report.py`, `tests/conftest.py`, `tests/test_probe.py`, `tests/test_publication.py`, `tests/test_report.py`, `tests/test_triage.py`, `tests/test_triage_data.py`, `tests/test_triage_experiment.py`, and `tests/test_exploratory_whole_pool.py`.
  
